## 1. Decision D-1: Column-Key Type Design

### Resolution of Open Questions
- **(Q1) Type Strategy:** Generic visual types (`TimedDragVisual<TColumnKey = string>`, `AllDayDragVisual<TColumnKey = string>`) parameterized by view-specific column key domain types (`DateColumnKey` for Week, `DayColumnKey` for Day).
- **(Q2) Day Module Structure:** Day interaction handlers are decomposed under [`packages/web/src/views/Day/interaction/adapter/interactions/`](file:///home/sainadh/projects/compass-calendar/compass/compass-calendar/packages/web/src/views/Day/interaction/adapter/interactions/) to match Week's structure 1:1.
- **(Q3) Shared Adapter Types Location:** Shared adapter types are placed in [`packages/web/src/grid/interaction/types/adapter.types.ts`](file:///home/sainadh/projects/compass-calendar/compass/compass-calendar/packages/web/src/grid/interaction/types/adapter.types.ts), preserving `grid/interaction/types/` as the contract home while [`packages/web/src/grid/interaction/adapter.helpers.ts`](file:///home/sainadh/projects/compass-calendar/compass/compass-calendar/packages/web/src/grid/interaction/adapter.helpers.ts) houses execution helpers.

### Justification Against Hard Constraints
1. **Day Runtime Fallback Union:** Day view column keys are runtime unions (`CalendarId[]` during multi-column calendar drag vs `[visibleDateKey]` date string fallback on single-column or resize). Because the fallback provides exactly one column, `visual.dayDate === visual.initialDayDate` is invariant, making `visual.dayDate !== visual.initialDayDate` strictly `false` and preventing `visual.dayDate as CalendarId` from ever evaluating on date strings in `columnMoveCalendarId`. Defining `type DayColumnKey = CalendarId | string` accurately models this runtime reality without unsound branded casts.
2. **Cross-Row Date Parsing Guarantee:** [`packages/web/src/grid/interaction/commit/cross-row.commit.ts`](file:///home/sainadh/projects/compass-calendar/compass/compass-calendar/packages/web/src/grid/interaction/commit/cross-row.commit.ts) performs `dayjs(visual.dayDate)`. By typing `timedDragVisualToAllDayGridEvent` and `allDayDragVisualToTimedGridEvent` to strictly accept `TimedDragVisual<DateColumnKey>` / `AllDayDragVisual<DateColumnKey>`, passing a Day visual (`TimedDragVisual<DayColumnKey>`) is a compile-time type error (`DayColumnKey` is not assignable to `DateColumnKey`).

### Proposed TypeScript Declarations

```typescript
// packages/web/src/grid/interaction/types/column-key.types.ts
import { type CalendarId } from "@core/types/domain-primitives";
export type DateColumnKey = string & { readonly __brand?: "DateColumnKey" };
export type DayColumnKey = CalendarId | string;

// packages/web/src/grid/interaction/types/timed-drag.types.ts
export interface TimedDragVisual<TColumnKey = string> {
  crossRowSize: CrossRowSize;
  dayDate: TColumnKey;
  dayIndex: number;
  durationMinutes: number;
  endMinutes: number;
  eventId: string;
  initialDayDate: TColumnKey;
  initialDayIndex: number;
  initialEndMinutes: number;
  initialStartMinutes: number;
  pointerStart: VisualPoint;
  row: DragRow;
  sourceRect: VisualRect;
  startMinutes: number;
  transform: VisualPoint;
  type: "timedDrag";
}

// packages/web/src/grid/interaction/types/all-day-drag.types.ts
export interface AllDayDragVisual<TColumnKey = string> {
  crossRowSize: CrossRowSize;
  dayDate: TColumnKey;
  dayIndex: number;
  eventId: string;
  initialDayDate: TColumnKey;
  initialDayIndex: number;
  pointerStart: VisualPoint;
  row: DragRow;
  sourceRect: VisualRect;
  timedStartMinutes: number | null;
  transform: VisualPoint;
  type: "allDayDrag";
}

// packages/web/src/views/Day/interaction/adapter/commit/timed.commit.ts
export const columnMoveCalendarId = (
  visual: Pick<TimedDragVisual<DayColumnKey>, "dayDate" | "initialDayDate">,
  event: GridEvent,
): CalendarId | undefined =>
  visual.dayDate !== visual.initialDayDate
    ? (visual.dayDate as CalendarId)
    : event.calendarId;
```

